- Yeah.

00:00:03.383 --> 00:00:04.554
- Is who the (beep) is this guy?

00:00:04.554 --> 00:00:05.387
- Yeah.

00:00:05.387 --> 00:00:06.269
- I mean, you get that, right?

00:00:06.269 --> 00:00:07.579
- [Gary] Of course.

00:00:07.579 --> 00:00:08.638
- Who the (beep) are you?

00:00:08.638 --> 00:00:11.305
(ambient music)

00:00:18.669 --> 00:00:21.104
- This is a word that is rarely
talked about in our space

00:00:21.104 --> 00:00:23.827
that I wanna start building
more attention for.

00:00:23.827 --> 00:00:25.593
Self-awareness.

00:00:25.593 --> 00:00:28.215
I wanna deliver on 
this message so much.

00:00:28.215 --> 00:00:30.590
I would create a test or a drug

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:32.833
that allowed people 
to become self-aware.

00:00:32.833 --> 00:00:35.590
One potion inject, 
not hustle, not smart.

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:37.149
Self-awareness.

00:00:37.149 --> 00:00:40.479
I don't fear being self-aware.

00:00:41.339 --> 00:00:43.658
I know I suck at a lot of stuff.

00:00:43.658 --> 00:00:46.688
I think everybody 
lies to themselves.

00:00:46.688 --> 00:00:49.298
Some people are meant
to be B and C players.

00:00:49.298 --> 00:00:50.981
And I'm pissed 
that the narrative now

00:00:50.981 --> 00:00:52.356
is that you need 
to be a number one

00:00:52.356 --> 00:00:53.581
and have your company.

00:00:53.581 --> 00:00:54.721
Because a lot of 
people are gonna lose

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:56.701
or leave money on the table,

00:00:56.701 --> 00:00:58.839
because that's just the narrative.

00:00:58.839 --> 00:00:59.945
'Cause I'm such a positive guy,

00:00:59.945 --> 00:01:02.905
I struggle to think about
the things I'm bad at,

00:01:02.905 --> 00:01:06.924
but self-awareness
requires understanding both

00:01:06.924 --> 00:01:09.013
and then choosing which
path you wanna go through.

00:01:09.013 --> 00:01:11.503
I'm a big fan of going
all in on your strengths.

00:01:11.503 --> 00:01:13.448
And don't give a fuck
about what you suck at.

00:01:13.448 --> 00:01:16.339
Self-awareness isn't only just
betting on your strengths,

00:01:16.339 --> 00:01:19.859
it's accepting all 
your shortcomings.

00:01:19.859 --> 00:01:20.838
Let me tell you one thing.

00:01:20.838 --> 00:01:23.875
What works for me does not
necessarily work for you.

00:01:23.875 --> 00:01:26.508
I think being at peace with
yourself and your skill set

00:01:26.508 --> 00:01:28.491
is such an important 
part of this.

00:01:28.491 --> 00:01:30.569
Too many people 
try to be like me,

00:01:30.569 --> 00:01:32.281
because it's sizzly 
and it's sexy,

00:01:32.281 --> 00:01:34.906
and people wanna be
charismatic and on stage.

00:01:34.906 --> 00:01:38.639
So many of you do so many
things better than I do.

00:01:38.639 --> 00:01:40.902
You can look at how people roll,

00:01:40.902 --> 00:01:43.320
and it's great to admire
and things of that nature,

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:47.956
but it's so damn important
to stick to your DNA.

00:01:47.956 --> 00:01:49.932
Try to get to a place where
you understand yourself

00:01:49.932 --> 00:01:51.642
and understand what 
your strengths are.

00:01:51.642 --> 00:01:53.153
You've gotta find 
your self-awareness.

00:01:53.153 --> 00:01:55.436
All your shortcomings
are there for a reason.

00:01:55.436 --> 00:01:57.774
They're there to also
allow you to be great.

00:01:57.774 --> 00:02:00.163
Deep in your brain, 
deep in your heart,

00:02:00.163 --> 00:02:02.454
you actually accept
all those shortcomings,

00:02:02.454 --> 00:02:05.276
is the second your life
goes on the offense.

00:02:05.276 --> 00:02:08.080
I worry that people don't
tap into their strengths.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:10.148
You have to audit 
who you actually are,

00:02:10.148 --> 00:02:11.683
because then you're not
gonna bullshit yourself.

00:02:11.683 --> 00:02:12.658
You're gonna story-tell yourself,

00:02:12.658 --> 00:02:14.019
you're gonna motivate yourself,

00:02:14.019 --> 00:02:15.550
but you're not gonna 
bullshit yourself.

00:02:15.550 --> 00:02:16.748
And once you believe that,

00:02:16.748 --> 00:02:18.923
either for yourself or
someone else told you,

00:02:18.923 --> 00:02:21.902
go directly all chips, 
all in to that.

00:02:21.902 --> 00:02:23.353
And we've all got something,

00:02:23.353 --> 00:02:25.077
and you just need to 
accept what's yours

00:02:25.077 --> 00:02:26.198
and go in on that.

00:02:26.198 --> 00:02:28.660
Then you've got a
starting point to success.

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:31.042
And so self-awareness 
at its finest

00:02:31.042 --> 00:02:33.191
is accepting your shortcomings

00:02:33.191 --> 00:02:35.818
and accentuating your strengths.

00:02:35.818 --> 00:02:37.156
- Who the (beep) are you?

00:02:37.156 --> 00:02:38.989
- I'm an entrepreneur.

